WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.617
SBOMs can strengthen vulnerability management by helping teams identify where affected components are used.

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:07.587
When a vulnerability is disclosed,

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:11.922
the first operational question is often whether the organization is exposed.

00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:16.651
Without component visibility, teams may need to search repositories, contact product owners,

00:00:16.651 --> 00:00:19.409
inspect builds, or wait for manual analysis.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:22.167
That can slow response when time matters.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.744
With usable SBOM data,

00:00:23.744 --> 00:00:28.078
teams can compare known vulnerable components and versions against software inventories.

00:00:28.078 --> 00:00:31.231
This can help identify affected products, prioritize investigation,

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.807
and focus remediation effort.

00:00:32.807 --> 00:00:37.142
SBOMs do not replace vulnerability scanning, patch management, secure coding, testing,

00:00:37.142 --> 00:00:38.324
or incident response.

00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:43.447
They complement those activities by improving the quality and speed of component-level visibility.

00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:45.023
Context is still necessary.

00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:50.540
A component may be present but not reachable, not used in a vulnerable way,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.510
or protected by other controls.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.845
Teams still need analysis to determine actual exposure and response priority.

00:00:56.845 --> 00:00:59.603
SBOMs can also support long-term vulnerability trends.

00:00:59.603 --> 00:01:03.150
Organizations can see which products depend on outdated components,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:08.273
where unsupported libraries remain, and which teams may need help reducing dependency risk.

00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:13.001
The best vulnerability management use cases connect SBOMs to ownership, deployment data,

00:01:13.001 --> 00:01:15.366
severity information, exploitability analysis, remediation workflows,

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.730
and verification that changes were completed.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.277
This connection is what turns inventory into response capability.

00:01:21.277 --> 00:01:26.005
An SBOM can show that a component exists, but ownership, deployment context,

00:01:26.005 --> 00:01:30.340
and remediation tracking help the organization decide what to do next.
